# ===========================================================================
# Google Workspace credentials for the Hermes agent. OPTIONAL add-on --
# nothing in the base build reads this file.
#
# Copied to config/google.env (0600) and installed into the VM at
# ~/.config/agent-sandbox/google.env, where the Hermes gateway reads it
# through a systemd EnvironmentFile. Never commit the filled-in copy, and
# never paste these values into a chat with an agent.
#
# You fill in the top two by hand. The bottom two are written for you by
#
#     ./scripts/addon-google-workspace.sh auth
#
# which opens a browser, asks you to consent, and writes the result here --
# plus a second file beside it, google-credentials-<your-address>.json, in
# the layout the MCP server reads. Both are gitignored and 0600. Consent
# happens on this machine because the VM has no browser.
# ===========================================================================

# --- From Google Cloud Console ----------------------------------------------
# Create an OAuth client of type "Desktop app" and copy both values here.
# See addons/google-workspace/README.md for the five steps, including the
# one that matters most: publish the consent screen. Left in "Testing", the
# refresh token below expires after seven days, every time.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# --- Written by `addon-google-workspace.sh auth` ----------------------------
# LEAVE BLANK. Filling these in by hand means copying a long secret through
# your clipboard for no reason; the auth command writes them directly.
#
# The refresh token is the actual key to the account. Everything else here
# identifies the app, not you.
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=""
# The account that consented. Written from Google's own userinfo response,
# so it is what the token really belongs to rather than what you expected.
GOOGLE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=""
